hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4870","It was narrated from An-Nu'man bin Bashir that:a group of the Kala'iyin complaned to him about some people who had stolen some goods"
"4871","It was narrated from abu Hurairah that the Prophet - and Ahmad said in his Hadith:\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'No one who commits Zina is a believer at the moment when he is committing Zina; no one who steals is a believer at the moment when he is stealing; no one who drinks wine is a believer at the moment when he is drinking it; but repentance is available to him after that."
"4872","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:\"No one who commits Zina is a believer at the moment when he is committing Zina; no one who steals is a believer at the moment when he is stealing; no one who drinks wine is a believer at the moment when he is drinking it.\" - And he mentioned a fourth but I (the narrator) have forgotten it - \"When he does that the yoke of Islam is shed from his neck, but if he repents, Allah accepts his repentance.\""
"4873","It was narrated from abu Umayah Al-Makhzumi that:a thief who confused to a crime but with whom no stolen goods has been found"
"4874","It was narrated from An-Nu'man bin Bashir that:a group of the Kala'iyin complaned to him about some people who had stolen some goods, shoe detained them for several days, and then he let them go. They came and said: \"You let them go without any pressure (to make them admit to their crime) or beating?\" An-Nu'man said: \"What do you want? If you wish, I will beat them, and if Allah brings back your goods thereby, all well and good. Otherwise I will take retaliation from your backs (by beating you) likewise.\" They said: \"is this your ruling?\" He said: \"This is the ruling of Allah and His Messenger \"(Daif)"
"4875","It was narrated from Safwan bin Umayyah that:a man stole his Burdah"
"4876","It was narrated from Bahz bin Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, that:the Messenger of Allah detained a man who was under suspicion, and then he let him go. (Hssan)"
"4877","It was narrated from Safwan bin Umayyah that:he circumambulated theKa'bah and prayed"
"4878","It narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\"\"Safwina was slleping in the Masjid with his Rida' beneath him"
"4879","It was knarrated that Safwan bin Umayyah said:\"\"I was sleeping in the Masjid on a Khmaishah of mine that was worth thirty dirhams"
"4880","It was narrated from Safwan bin Umayyah that:a Khamisah was stolen from beneath his head while he slept in the Masjid of the Prophet. He caught there thief and brought him to the Prophet"
"4881","It was narrated from Safwan bin Umayyah that:he circumambulated theKa'bah and prayed, then he rolled up a Rid' of his and placed it beneath his head, and slept. A thief came and slid it out from beneath his head and took it. He brought him to the Prophet and said: \"This man stole my Rida. The Prophet said to him: Did you steal this man's Rida?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Take him away and cut his hand off.\" Safwan said: \"I* did not want to have his hand cut off for my Rida'.\" He said: \"Why (did you not say that) before now?\""
"4882","It narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\"Safwina was slleping in the Masjid with his Rida' beneath him, and it was stolen. He got up, and the man had gone, but he caught up with him, and took him to the prophet, who ordered that his hand be cut off. Safwan said; 'O Messenger of Allah, my Rida 'is not worth cutting off a man's hand for. 'He said 'Why did you not say that before you brought him to me"
"4883","It was knarrated that Safwan bin Umayyah said:\"I was sleeping in the Masjid on a Khmaishah of mine that was worth thirty dirhams, and a man came and stole it from me. The man was caught and taken to the Prophet, who ordered that his hand be cut off. I came to him and said: \"Will you cut off his hand for the sake of only thirty Dirhams? I will sell it to him on credit.\" He said:\" Why did you not say this before you brought him to me?\""
"4884","It was narrated from Safwan bin Umayyah that:a Khamisah was stolen from beneath his head while he slept in the Masjid of the Prophet. He caught there thief and brought him to the Prophet, who ordered that his hand be cut off. Safwan said: \"Are you going to cut off his hand?\" He said \"Why didn't you let him go before you b brought him to me?\" (Daif)"
"4885","It was narrated form 'Amr bin Shu'ainb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet said:\"Pardon matters that may deserve a Hadd punishment before you bring it to my attention, for whatever is brought to my attention, the Hadd punishment becomes binding.\" (Saif)"
"4886","It was narrated from Nafi that:a woman used to borrow jewelry during the time of the Messenger of Allah. She borrowed some jewelry"
"4887","It was narrated from Jabir that:a woman from Banu Makhzum stole (something)"
"4888","It was narrated from Saeed bin AL-Musayyab that:a woman from Banu Makhzum borrowed some jewelry"
"4889","It was narrated from Dawud bin Abi Asim that:Saeed bin Al-Musayyb narrated something similar to that"
"4890","Sufyan said:\"\"There was a Makhzumi woman who used to borrow things then deny that. She was brought to the Messenger of Allah and he was told about her. He said: 'If it were Fatimah (who stole)"
"4891","It was narrated from `A'ishah that:A woman stole (something) and she was brought to the Prophet. They said: \"\"Who would dare to speak to the Messenger of Allah except Usamah.\"\" So they spoke to Usamah and he spoke to (the Prophet). The Prophet said: \"\"O Usamah"
"4892","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:\"\"A thief was brought to the hand.\"\" They said: \"\"We did not think that you would take it so far.\"\" He said: \"\"If it were Fatimah (who stole)"
"4893","It was narrated from 'Aishah that:a woman stole at the time of Messenger of Allah and they said: \"\"We cannot speak to him concerning her; there is no one who can speak to him except his beloved"
"4894","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:\"\"A woman borrowed some jewelry"
"4895","It was narrated from 'Aishah that Quraish were worried about the Mkahzumi woman who had stolen. They said; Who will speak to the Messenger of Allah concerning her?\"\" They said:\"\"Who would dare to do that except Usamah bin Zaid"
"4896","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:\"A thief was brought to the hand.\" They said: \"We did not think that you would take it so far.\" He said: \"If it were Fatimah (who stole), I would cut off her hand.\""
"4897","It was narrated from 'Aishah the Quraish were worried about the case of the Makhzumi woman who stole"
"4898","It was narrated from 'Aishah that:a woman stole at the time of the Messenger of Allah"
"4899","It was narrated that Az-Zuhri said:\"\"Urwah bin Az-Zubair told me that a woman stole at the time of the Messenger of Allah"
"4900","Abu Hurairah said:\"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'A Hadd punishment that is carried out on earth is better for the people of earth than if it were to rain for thirty mornings.\"\"' (Daif)"
"4901","It was narrated that Abu Zurah said:\"\"Abu Hurairah said: 'Carrying out a Hadd punishment in a land is better for its people than if it were to rain for forty nights.\"\" (Daif)"
"4902","Abdullah bin 'Amr said:\"\"The Messenger of Allah cut off (a thief's hand) for a shield which was worth five Durham's.\"\" This is how he (the narrator) said it. (Daif)"
"4903","Abdullah bin 'Umar said:\"\"The Messenger of Allah cut off (a thief's hand) for a shield which was worth three Dirham.\"\" (Sahih) Abu 'Abdur-Rahman (An-Nasai) said: This is correct"
"4904","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that:the Messenger of Allah cut off (a thief's hand) for a shield which cost three Dirhams"
"4905","Abdullah bin 'Umar narrated that:the Prophet cut off the hand of a thief"
"4906","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that:the Messenger of Allah cut off (a thief's hand) for a shield that was worth three Dirhams"
"4907","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that:the Messenger of Allah cut off (a thief's hand) for a shield. (Sahih) Abu 'Abdur-Rahman (An-Nasai) said: This is a mistake"
"4908","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that:the Messenger of Allah cut off (a thief's hand) for a shield which cost three Dirhams."
"4909","It was narrated that Qatadah said:\"\"I heard Anas say: 'A man stole a shield during the time of Abu Bakr"
"4910","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that: the Messenger of Allah cut off (a thief's hand) for a shield that was worth three Dirhams."
"4911","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:\"\"(The thief's hand) is not to be cut off except for the price of a shield"
"4912","It was narrated that Anas said:\"Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, cut off (a thief's hand) for a shield that was worth five Dirhams."
"4913","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:\"\"The hand of the thief is to be cut off for a quarter of a Dinar"
"4914","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Prophet said:\"\"The hand of the thief is to be cut off for one-quarter of a Dinar or more"
"4915","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:\"\"The hand of the thief is to be cut off for one-quarter of a Dinar or more"
"4916","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said:\"\"The hand of the thief is to be cut off for one-quarter of a Dinar or more"
"4917","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah\"\" (one of the narrators) Qutaibah said:'Used to cut off the hand of the thief for one-quarter of a Dinar or more"
"4918","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Prophet said:\"The hand of the thief is to be cut off for one-quarter of a Dinar or more.\""
"4919","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah said: \"The hand of the thief is to be cut off for one-quarter of a Dinar or more.\""
"4920","It was narrated from 'Amrah that she heard 'Aishah say:\"\"The hand of the thief is to be cut off for one-quarter of a Dinar or more.\"\" (Sahih) Abu 'Abdur-Rahman (An-Nasai) said: This is the correct version of the narration of Yahya"
"4921","It was narrated from 'Amrah that she heard 'Aishah say:\"\"The hand of the thief is to be cut off for one-quarter of a Dinar or more"
"4922","It was narrated from 'Amrah that 'Aishah said:\"\"Cutting off (the hand of the thief) is for one-quarter of a Dinar or more"
"4923","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:\"\"It has not been too long and I have not forgotten yet. Cutting off (the hand of the thief) is for one-quarter of a Dinar or more"
"4924","It was narrated from 'Aishah that:she heard the Messenger of Allah say: \"\"The hand of the thief is not be cut off except for one-quarter of a Dinar or more"
"4925","Narrator mentioned in hadith:A similar report was narrated from 'Aishah from the Messenger of Allah"
"4926","It was narrated that 'Amrah said:\"\"Aishah said: 'Cutting off (the hand of the thief) is for one-quarter of a Dinar or more"
"4927","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:\"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'The hand of the thief is to be cut off for the price of a shield"
"4928","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:\"\"The Messenger of Allah used to cut off the (thief's) hand for one-quarter of a Dinar or more"
"4929","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:\"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'The hand (of the thief) is not to be cut off except for one-quarter of a Dinar"
"4930",""
"4931","Aishah said:The Messenger of Allah said: 'The hand of the thief is not to be cut off for anything less than a shield.\"\"' It was said to 'Aishah: 'What is the price of a shield?\"\" She said: \"\"One-quarter of a Dinar"
"4932","It was narrated from 'Aishah that she heard the Messenger of Allah say:\"\"The hand of a thief is not to be cut off except for one-quarter of a Dinar or more"
"4933","Makhramah narrated that his father said:\"\"I heard 'Uthman bin Abi AL-Walid"
"4934","Uthman bin Abi Al-Walid said:\"\"I heard 'Urwah bin Az-Zubair say: \"\"Aishah used to narrate that he Prophet of Allah said: The hand (of the thief) should not be cut off except for a shield or its equivalent in value. And he said that 'Urwah said: A shield is (worth) four Dirhams. And he (the narrator) said: I heard sulaiman bin Yasar say that he heard 'Amrah say: I heard 'Aishah narrate that she heard the Messenger of Allah say: The hand (of the thief) should not be cut off except for four Dinars or more"
"4935","Uthman bin Abi Al-Walid said:\"\"I heard 'Urwah bin Az-Zubair say: \"\"Aishah used to narrate that he Prophet of Allah said: The hand (of the thief) should not be cut off except for a shield or its equivalent in value. And he said that 'Urwah said: A shield is (worth) four Dirhams. And he (the narrator) said: I heard sulaiman bin Yasar say that he heard 'Amrah say: I heard 'Aishah narrate that she heard the Messenger of Allah say: The hand (of the thief) should not be cut off except for four Dinars or more"
"4936","It was narrated that sulaiman bin Yasar said:\"\"Five (fingers i.e."
"4937","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:\"\"The hand of the thief should not be cut off for anything less than a Hajafah or a Turs (two kinds of shields)"
"4938","It was narrated from 'Abdullah that:the Prophet cut off (the thief's hand) for (something) that was worth five Dirhams. (Daif)"
"4940","It was narrated that Ayman said:\"\"The Prophet did not cut off the (hand of) the thief except for the value of a shield"
"4941","It was narrated that Ayman said:\"\"The hand of a thief would not be cut off during the time of the Messenger of Allah except for the value of a shield"
"4942","It was narrated that Ayman said:\"\"The hand of a thief was not be cut off during the time of the Messenger of Allah except for the value of a shield"
"4943","It was narrated that Ayman said:\"\"The hand of a thief was not be cut off during the time of the Messenger of Allah except for the price of a shield"
"4944","It was narrated that Ayman said:\"\"The (hand of) a thief is to be cut off for the price of a shield"
"4945","It was narrated that Ayman bin Umm Ayman who attributed it to the Prophet said:\"\"The (hand of) a thief is not to be cut off except for the price of a shield"
"4946","It was narrated that Ayman said:\"\"The (hand of) a thief is not to be cut off for less than the price of a shield.\"\" (Daif Mawquf)"
"4947",""
"4948","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:A similar report was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas. The price of a shield at the time of the Messenger of Allah was estimated to be ten Dirhams"
"4949","Narrated from Ayyub bin Musa:(A similar report) was narrated from Ayyub bin Musa"
"4950","It was narrated that 'Ata' said:\"\"The least for which the hand of a thief is to be cut off is the price of a shield. And the price of a shield in those days was ten Dirhams.\"\" (Hasan) Abu 'Abdur-Rahman (An-Nasai) said: Ayman"
"4951","It was narrated that Ka'b said:\"\"Whoever performs wudu and performs wudu"
"4952","It was narrated that Ka'b said:\"\"Whoever performs Wudu and performs Wudu well"
"4953","It was narrated that 'Ata' said:\"The least for which the hand of a thief is to be cut off is the price of a shield. And the price of a shield in those days was ten Dirhams.\" (Hasan) Abu 'Abdur-Rahman (An-Nasai) said: Ayman, the one whose narrations preceded, I do not think he was a Companion, and another Hadith has been related from him which proves what we have said:"
"4954",""
"4955","It was narrated that Ka'b said:\"Whoever performs Wudu and performs Wudu well, then attends Isha prayer in congregation, then prays four similar Rakahs after that, reciting therein and bowing and prostrating perfectly, that will bring him a reward like that of (praying) Lailat Al-Qadar.\" (Hasan Maqtu)"
"4956","It was narrated from 'Amr bin Shuaib, from his father, that his grandfather said:\"The price of a shield at the time of the Messenger of Allah was ten Dirhams.\""
"4957","It was narrated that Rafi bin Khadij said:\"\"I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'The hand is not to be cut off for (stealing) produce or the spadix of palm trees"
"4958","It was narrated that Rafi bin Khadij said:\"\"I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'The hand is not to be cut off for (stealing) produce or the spadix of palm trees"
"4959","It was narrated that Rafi bin Khadij said:\"\"I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'The hand is not to be cut off for (stealing) produce or the spadix of palm trees"
"4960","It was narrated that Rafi bin Khadij said:\"\"I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'The hand is not to be cut off for (stealing) produce or the spadix of palm trees"
"4961","It was narrated that Rafi bin Khadij said:\"\"I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'The hand is not to be cut off for (stealing) produce or the spadix of palm trees"
"4962","It was narrated that Rafi bin Khadij said:\"\"I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'The hand is not to be cut off for (stealing) produce or the spadix of palm trees"
"4963","It was narrated that Rafi bin Khadij said:\"\"I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'The hand is not to be cut off for (stealing) produce or the spadix of palm trees"
"4964","Rafi bin Khadij said:\"\"I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'The hand is not be cut off for (stealing) produce or the spadix of palm trees"
"4965","It was narrated that Rafi bin Khadij said:\"\"I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'The hand is not to be cut off for (stealing) produce or the spadix of palm trees.\"\"' (Sahih) Abu 'Abdur-Rahman (An-Nasai) said: This is a mistake"
"4966","It was narrated that Rafi bin Khadij said:\"\"I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'The hand is not to be cut off for (stealing) produce or the spadix of palm trees"
"4967","It was narrated that Rafi bin Khadij said:\"\"I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'The hand is not to be cut off for (stealing) produce or the spadix of palm trees"
"4968","It was narrated that Rafi bin Khadij said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'The hand is not to be cut off for (stealing) produce or the spadix of palm trees.\"' (Sahih) Abu 'Abdur-Rahman (An-Nasai) said: This is a mistake, and I do not know who Abu Maimun (one of the narrators) is."
"4969","It was narrated that Rafi bin Khadij said:\"I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'The hand is not to be cut off for (stealing) produce or the spadix of palm trees.\"'"
"4970","It was narrated from Jabir that the Messenger of Allah said:\"\"The hand of the pilferer is not to be cut off"
"4971","It was narrated from Hajjaj from Ibn Juraij from Abu Az-Zubair"
"4972","It was narrated that Jabir said:\"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'The hand of the pilferer"
"4973","It was narrated that Jabir said:\"\"The hand of the traitor is not to be cut off.\"\" (Sahih) Abu 'Abdur-Rahman (An-Nasai) said: Ashath bin Sawwar (one of its narrators) is weak"
"4974","It was narrated from Al-Harith bin Hatib that a thief was brought to the Messenger of Allah and he said:\"\"Kill him.\"\" They said: \"\"O Messenger of Allah"
"4975","It was narrated that Jabir bin 'Abdullah said:\"\"A thief was brought to the Messenger of Allah and he said: 'Kill him.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"4976","It was narrated that Junadah bin Abi Umayyah said:\"\"I heard Busr bin Abi Artah say: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah say: Hand should not be cut off while traveling"
"4977","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet said:\"\"If a slave steals"
"4978","It was narrated that 'Atiyyah said:'I was among the prisoners of Quraizah; we were examined"
"4979","It was narrated that Ibn Muhairiz said; \"\"I asked Fadalah bin 'Ubaid about hanging the hand (of the thief) from his neck"
"4980","It was narrated that 'Abdur-Rahman bin Muhairiz said:\"\"I said to Fadalah bin 'Ubaid: 'Do you think that hanging the hand from the thief's neck is Sunnah?' He said: 'Yes; a thief was brought to the Messenger of Allah and he cut off his hand and hung it from his neck.\"\"' (Daif) Abu 'Abdur-Rahman (An-Nasai) said; Al-Hajjaj bin Artah is weak"
"4981","It was narrated from 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Awf that the Messenger of Allah said:\"\"The thief is not to be penalized (financially) if the Hadd punishment is carried out on him.\"\" (Daif) Abu 'Abdur-Rahman (An-Nasai) said: This is Mursal and it is not confirmed"
"4982","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that:The Messenger of Allah [SAW] was asked: \"\"Which deed is best?\"\" \"\"He said: Faith in Allah [SWT] and His messenger [SAW]"
"4983","It was narrated from Abdullah bin Hubshi Al-Khath'ami that:The Prophet [SAW] was asked: \"\"Which deed is best?\"\" He said: \"\"Faith in which there is no doubt"
"4984","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:\"\"The messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'There are three things"
